# Sender-domain allowlist for inbound mail to this triage mailbox
# (phishing@pwned.email). Loaded by postfix-main.cf's
# dms_smtpd_sender_restrictions override.
#
# Format: Postfix access-map entries, one per line - "domain  OK".
# Postfix matches parent domains automatically (e.g. an entry for
# "33k.org" also matches mail from user@mail.33k.org). Any sender domain
# NOT listed here is rejected outright - this is an allowlist, not a
# denylist, by design (see the conversation that added this: the ask was
# specifically "everything else is deny").
#
# This does NOT restrict what the attacker/lookalike domain inside a
# forwarded phishing email can be - that's the whole point of this
# mailbox. It only restricts who can forward mail to us in the first
# place (i.e. the outer envelope sender - real employees).
33k.org OK
